error[E0086]: 'v1' has no initializer, so its type cannot be inferred; a `let` binding without an initializer requires a type annotation (§10.1)
  --> check_let_binding_needs_type.bit:16:7
   |
16 |   let v1, ok1 = m["a"]
   |       ^^ give it a type, e.g. `let v1: <type>`; a two-result map read is `let (v, ok) = m[k]` (§12.6), not `let v, ok = m[k]`
error[E0086]: 'a1' has no initializer, so its type cannot be inferred; a `let` binding without an initializer requires a type annotation (§10.1)
  --> check_let_binding_needs_type.bit:17:7
   |
17 |   let a1, b1 = 1
   |       ^^ give it a type, e.g. `let a1: <type>`; a two-result map read is `let (v, ok) = m[k]` (§12.6), not `let v, ok = m[k]`
